  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }6\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x))=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14189988/assets/873a6fb793d2ae68eab172132e467a48a43ab84733ad92155fe6cc012f516382.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }6\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3-2x))=6\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})=3\\pi .\n$$",
